# Component Builder

Next.js App Router app: chat sidebar (left) + generated code panel (right).

## Architecture

```
app/page.tsx          → layout shell, shared state (code, componentName)
components/           → ChatSidebar, CodePanel, MessageBubble (client components)
app/api/generate/     → server route for AI code generation
lib/                  → prompt builders, SDK/Gemini helpers
```

- Keep API keys (`CURSOR_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) in `.env.local` — never expose to the client.
- All AI calls go through `app/api/generate/route.ts`, not from browser components.

## Cursor SDK (code generation)

Use `@cursor/sdk` server-side for one-shot component generation:

```typescript
import { Agent } from "@cursor/sdk";

const result = await Agent.prompt(buildPrompt(userMessage), {
  apiKey: process.env.CURSOR_API_KEY!,
  model: { id: "composer-2.5" },
  local: { cwd: process.cwd() },
});
```

- Prefer `Agent.prompt` for single-request generation; use `Agent.create` + `agent.send` only for multi-turn.
- Strip markdown fences from responses before displaying code.
- Return `{ code, componentName }` from the API route.

## Next.js patterns

- `"use client"` only on interactive components (`ChatSidebar`, `CodePanel`).
- API routes stay server-only; use `NextRequest` / `NextResponse`.
- Lift generated code state to `page.tsx`; pass down via props/callbacks.

## UI conventions

- Dark theme with Tailwind (`bg-gray-900`, `bg-gray-950`, `violet-600` accents).
- Sidebar: `overflow-x-hidden`, message bubbles use `break-words min-w-0` (no horizontal scroll).
- Send button disabled when `!input.trim()` or `isLoading`.
- Code panel: syntax highlighting + copy-to-clipboard with feedback.

## Generated component rules

Prompt the agent to return:
- Valid TSX with Tailwind CSS only
- Named export (`export function ComponentName`)
- First line: `// ComponentName`
- No markdown fences or explanations in output

## Error handling

- Retry transient failures (503, 429, `fetch failed`) with backoff.
- Return short, user-friendly errors in chat — never dump raw API URLs.
- Distinguish: missing key, invalid key, model unavailable, network/high demand.
